.TH EVENT_LOOP_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
event_loop_destroy \- destroy an event_loop and set handle to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

event_loop_destroy(loop);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls __event_loop_destroy() to shut the reactor thread down (if not
already shut down) and free every remaining registration, then sets loop
to NULL.

See __event_loop_destroy(3) for the queue-outlives-the-loop safety
guarantee this provides for queue-backed registrations.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  event_loop variable to destroy (set to NULL after destruction).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call with a NULL handle (no-op).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR __event_loop_destroy (3),
.BR event_loop_create (3),
.BR event_loop_shutdown (3)
